# Pathfinder 1e OGL — What Is Safe & Separation Rules

This project uses game mechanics from the Pathfinder Roleplaying Game, which are Open Game Content under the OGL v1.0a.

## Core Principle

Per the Pathfinder Core Rulebook OGL declaration: all **game mechanics** are Open Game Content (OGC). Product Identity (PI) is **not** Open Game Content.

## Open Game Content (safe to implement)

The following mechanical elements are OGC and may be implemented in code and data structures:

- Skill systems and calculations
- Ability score modifiers
- Race mechanics (bonuses, penalties, traits)
- Class progression tables (mechanical parts)
- Combat math (BAB, saves, AC formulas, etc.)
- Feat mechanics (not flavor text)
- Spell mechanics (not descriptive prose)
- Conditions and status effects (mechanical effects)

**Mechanics-only code does not require copying expressive text.** Avoid copying descriptive prose verbatim from the rulebook.

## Product Identity (do NOT use)

The following are explicitly Product Identity and cannot be reused without permission:

- Trademarks (Pathfinder, Paizo logo, etc.)
- Proper names tied to setting
- Deities
- Named characters
- Golarion-specific lore
- Storylines and plot text
- Dialogue
- Artwork
- Trade dress

## Directory Separation

Maintain strict separation between:

| Directory / Layer | Classification |
|---|---|
| `rules/` (mechanics data) | Potentially OGC |
| App logic (controllers, services, contexts) | Product Identity |
| Story content (seeds, narrative text) | Product Identity |
| UI/UX, branding, layouts | Product Identity |

1. **Mechanical data belongs in `rules/`** (e.g. [pathfinder_skills.ts](mdc:app/javascript/rules/pathfinder_skills.ts)). Never inline mechanical data tables into component logic, controllers, or service objects.
2. **Components read from `rules/` at runtime.** They do not embed OGC text themselves.
3. **The `/legal` route and its view are sacred.** Do not gate them behind authentication, do not dynamically alter the OGL text, and do not remove Section 15 entries. See [index.html.erb](mdc:app/views/legal/index.html.erb).
4. **Keep all lore and story content original.** Never copy setting-specific narrative from the rulebook.
